   "meaning": "Emu",
   "story": "Tchingal, the emu of the Boorong (Lake Tyrrell, Victoria), recorded by William Stanbridge in 1857 as a dark space near the Cross. The outline is the approximate RA/Dec polygon traced for Stellarium by John Morieson and Alex Cherney, running from the Coalsack through the dark lanes of the Milky Way towards Scorpius. The widely known Emu in the Sky is documented in other Aboriginal communities (e.g. Euahlayi and Kamilaroi; Fuller, Norris and Trudgett 2014, Australian Aboriginal astronomy); those community datasets are not included here."
